    'changelog' => 'v1.1.7 (2026-06-20): CORS-block UX — when gateway script loads or suggest fetches are blocked by the browser, storefronts show an inline notice where the dropdown would appear (seekmodo_cors_notice.js, bundle onerror, seekmodo-suggest:cors-blocked listener; @seekmodo/web-components v0.2.2). Also indexes `purchasable` alongside `in_stock` in numinix_seekmodo_push_catalog.php — backorder-eligible OOS (STOCK_ALLOW_CHECKOUT) stays purchasable; discontinued / call-for-price / optional NPF out_of_stock forced-OOS are not. RemoteConfig caches indexer_overrides from tenant.snapshot for NPF column name. - v1.1.6 fix LTR click attribution on Zen Cart 1.5.8+ storefronts that render search results at main_page=search_result (Numinix.com). referrerIsLocalSerp() and the SERP sendBeacon hook now recognise search_result / FILENAME_SEARCH_RESULT in addition to advanced_search_result, so product-page clicks from the live SERP are no longer silently dropped. - v1.1.4 (2026-06-19): shadow-mode LTR click attribution for competitor SERPs (Klevu). Successful shadow searches now stash search_event_id + rank map + SERP impressions; product-info referer attribution fires for local SERP clicks even when the clicked SKU is outside the shadow rank map; advanced_search_result pages emit a sendBeacon click hook for competitor-rendered grids. Adds catalog/numinix_seekmodo_click.php endpoint. - v1.1.3 (2026-06-17): test release for in-plugin Update verification (Connect page + Seekmodo Updates apply path; no functional connector changes). - v1.1.2 (2026-06-17): Connect page Update button when a newer release is published; GitSyncTrigger invokes cron/sync-to-git.sh immediately after in-plugin apply on git-enabled hosts; propagate_branches cherry-picks documented in zencart_git. - v1.1.1 (2026-06-15): suggest dropdown default min-width 320 -> 480 px (refreshes the vendored `@seekmodo/web-components` bundle to v0.2.1). Catalog-grade product names like `Handy Standard SBC990 Snowmobile Lift` and `Redline TR1500 Trailer` were truncating at ~15 chars in the typeahead dropdown when the storefront search input was the typical ~280 px width; the 480 default now fits ~35 chars of name + price column + thumbnail without wrapping. A new viewport-right clamp keeps the dropdown from painting off-screen on narrow mobile viewports (rendered width caps at `viewport.right - input.left - 8 px`). No PHP / schema / behaviour change beyond the vendored JS asset swap. - v1.1.0 (2026-06-14): adopts the new shared PHP SDK (`numinix/seekmodo-connector ^0.2`) as a vendored Composer dependency under `catalog/includes/library/Numinix/SeekmodoSdk/`. Legacy `Numinix\Seekmodo\*` classes stay in place as thin adapters so the storefront and admin behaviour are unchanged. - v1.0.22 (2026-06-13): SM-606 universal-suggest plumbing fixup. v1.0.21 shipped the new `<seekmodo-suggest>` bundle but FOUR independent bugs in the plumbing meant the new dropdown never rendered on any storefront and shoppers continued to see the legacy search UX: (1) bundle URL pointed at the live template tree where ZC\'s plugin loader does NOT merge static assets, so the bundle 404/406\'d everywhere; (2) the public `numinix_seekmodo_client()` function the observer and shims gate on via `function_exists()` was never written — the library only exposed `_numinix_seekmodo_client()` (underscore-prefixed), so the inline browser-token mint silently emitted `<meta name="seekmodo:token" content="">` and the refresh-URL shim returned 503 `{"error":"unpaired"}` even when the storefront was paired; (3) the catalog-root PHP shims lived only inside the plugin tree, but ZC\'s stock `zc_plugins/.htaccess` denies direct HTTP access to *.php under zc_plugins/, so the shim URLs 302-redirected to the storefront home; (4) the browser-token mint path called `Client::callTool(\'tenants/token\', …)` but `callTool()`\'s tool-name regex (^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{2,128}$) intentionally rejects slashes — the gateway exposes `/v1/tenants/token` as a non-tool admin endpoint (Sprint 7 PR 2), not a tool — so the call short-circuited to null and surfaced as `{"error":"mint_failed"}` from the shim. v1.0.22 fixes all four: bundleSrc() emits `/catalog/zc_plugins/Seekmodo/v1.0.22/catalog/.../seekmodo_suggest.bundle.js` (`.js` is allowlisted by zc_plugins/.htaccess); `numinix_seekmodo_client.php` now exports a public `numinix_seekmodo_client()` wrapper aliasing `_numinix_seekmodo_client()`; tenant repos ship the four catalog-root PHP shims (`numinix_seekmodo_suggest.php`, `numinix_seekmodo_recommend.php`, `numinix_seekmodo_pair_callback.php`, `numinix_seekmodo_forget_me.php`) alongside the rest of the storefront tree via their existing rsync-from-git pipelines; `Client::mintBrowserToken(int $ttlSeconds = 300, string $sid = \'\')` is a new public method that POSTs `/v1/tenants/token` directly via the same HMAC envelope, bypassing the tool-name regex. As defensive belt-and-suspenders the in-plugin shims gained a `__DIR__`-rooted application_top.php resolver + chdir() to the catalog root; this is a no-op at the live catalog root and makes the shim runnable from any nested location. No config, schema, or behavior change beyond making the v1.0.21 universal-suggest UX actually render. - v1.0.21 (2026-06-12): SM-606 Universal Suggest Widget — storefront typeahead now ships the new `<seekmodo-suggest>` web component (rich /v1/suggest envelope: recent + did_you_mean + keywords + trending + products + categories + "View all N results" CTA, all from one server round-trip). Same component the WordPress / BigCommerce / AKS connectors enqueue, so a tenant with multiple storefronts gets a single suggestions UX. Replaces the v1.0.14-era three-section vanilla-JS dropdown; the legacy code is preserved on disk at `seekmodo_typeahead.legacy.js` and enabled via `NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_SUGGEST_USE_LEGACY` (default false) for one major-version cycle so a site with bespoke CSS tied to the old dropdown markup can defer the swap. `catalog/numinix_seekmodo_suggest.php` stays as the REST proxy the bundle falls back to when the gateway-direct browser-token mint is unavailable (no behavior change). New `NuminixSeekmodoSuggestObserver` emits the SDK\'s `<meta name="seekmodo:tenant|gateway|refresh|token">` tags via `NOTIFY_HTML_HEAD_END`, mints the gateway-direct token via `Client::tenantToken`, then injects the bundle `<script src>` + a tiny inline autoboot that walks the same `input[name="keyword"]`, `#keyword`, `[data-seekmodo-typeahead]` selectors the legacy JS auto-attached to. KIP\'s `numinix_seekmodo_suggest.php` catalog-root override (the per-token multi-recall blend) is now redundant — WS-2 absorbed the same logic into `SuggestTool::loadTypesenseBlocks` so the bespoke shim can be deleted on the next KIP push. Bundle size: 22.6 KB raw / 7.25 KB gzip (under the 12 KB plan target). - v1.0.20 (2026-06-11): typeahead-perf parity with WordPress connector v0.5.0 (SM-602 phase B). Drops the per-keystroke WordPress-style fallback that re-ran the entire suggest payload on backspace + retype: the storefront-side typeahead JS now keeps a 32-entry LRU cache keyed on (vertical, max, normalized q), so a fast typist round-tripping `boa -> boat -> boa` only pays one network call. Adds a `lastQ` guard around the abort-controller dance so a slow-arriving keystroke for `boa` doesn\'t overwrite the freshly-rendered `boat` rows. JS-only change (no server schema or PHP behaviour shifts), implements phase B of the connector typeahead spec at seekmodo/docs/CONNECTOR_TYPEAHEAD_SPEC.md. Phase C (browser-token gateway-direct fetch, skip the PHP hop) is deferred to v1.0.21 because the Zen Cart connector doesn\'t mint browser tokens at page render today; the flat-rows-shape /v1/typeahead path is queued behind it as well. - v1.0.19 (2026-06-11): category landing-page redirect (Klevu / Algolia parity). A shopper query that closely matches a single storefront category now redirects to that category landing page instead of rendering an advanced_search_result SERP — same intent-aware behaviour competitive platforms have shipped for years. Matching is deliberately conservative: an order-invariant token match floor (0.92 default) plus a clear-winner gap (0.05 default) so the connector only redirects when there is genuinely no ambiguity. Resolver lives in includes/functions/numinix_seekmodo_category_redirect_lib.php; observer hook is NOTIFY_HEADER_START_ADVANCED_SEARCH_RESULTS so the redirect short-circuits Zen Cart\'s search SQL build, the swap-point gateway call, AND the SERP impression beacon. Per-tenant kill-switch at NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_CATEGORY_REDIRECT_ENABLED (default true), mirrored from admin.seekmodo.com -> tenant settings -> Category Redirect. Active-category list + per-query resolver result both APCu-cached so the hot-path cost is a single APCu fetch on a warm cache. Queries that arrive with structured narrowing filters (categories_id, manufacturers_id, price range, date range) are skipped so an explicit category-scoped search never silently widens to a different category page. - v1.0.18 (2026-06-09): stable signing key rotation (seekmodo-2026-06). - v1.0.17 (2026-06-08): AKS-connector parity — generic improvements ported from the AKS Sprint 2 / Sprint 8 (v1.3) release. (1) SKU exact-match boost: when the shopper\'s query looks like a SKU / part number (alphanumeric + dashes/underscores/dots, 2-32 chars by default), the connector sets prioritize_exact_match=true on the gateway call so the matching SKU floats to position 0 regardless of textual relevance scoring. Configurable via NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_SKU_BOOST_ENABLED (default true) and NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_SKU_BOOST_TRIGGER_REGEX. Applies to the full-search path AND the legacy /v1/search-based typeahead fallback. (2) Expanded tenant-unavailable graceful degradation: the storefront now falls back to native Zen Cart LIKE search on the full set of gateway tenant-lifecycle 4xx codes (tenant_paused, tenant_not_found, tenant_unknown, tenant_suspended, tenant_disabled — all 403 AND 404), not just the legacy 403 tenant_paused / subscription_cancelled / unknown_tenant subset. Structured client log line is emitted as `tenant_unavailable` with a `fallback_reason` field for distinct admin observability. Mirrors AKS connector v1.3\'s ClientException::TENANT_UNAVAILABLE_ERROR_CODES contract. - v1.0.16 (2026-06-05): per-shopper personalization plumbing. Adds the first-party sm_pid cookie (random 22-char URL-safe id, 1-year TTL, SameSite=Lax, behind NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_PERSONALIZATION_COOKIE_ENABLED for cookie-consent gating on EU storefronts; default off). Search, recommend, and event calls now stamp shopper_context.{customer_id, shopper_pid, do_not_personalize} so the gateway-side ShopperContextResolver can decide whether to apply the tenant\'s personalized model. The Do-Not-Personalize HTTP header (sent verbatim to the gateway when present on the inbound storefront request) and a per-customer ?seekmodo_forget_me=1 deeplink (signed-callback to admin.seekmodo.com -> tenant.shopper.forget) give shoppers a clear opt-out and right-to-be-forgotten surface their existing privacy page can link to. None of this adds new metering — personalization piggybacks on the existing search / recommend billing per §6.5 of SEARCH_FEATURES_PLAN.md. - v1.0.15 (2026-06-04): storefront recommendation + AI product bundle widgets — adds a new Client::recommend() method, a numinix_seekmodo_recommend() global helper, the storefront-side numinix_seekmodo_recommend.php AJAX endpoint, the jscript_seekmodo_recommendations.js auto-attach JS module (zero-config rendering for <div data-seekmodo-placement="..."> placeholders), and observer hooks (NOTIFY_FOOTER_END / NOTIFY_HEADER_END_SHOPPING_CART) that inject placement divs into the PDP / cart / home / category templates. Each rendered widget bills exactly one `searches` token (humans-only — bot keystrokes are excluded gateway-side) and lands in the `searches_recommend` display bucket on admin.seekmodo.com -> Usage. The whole feature is gated behind NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_RECOMMENDATIONS_ENABLED (default false). - v1.0.14 (2026-06-04): typeahead now routes through the gateway\'s dedicated SuggestTool (/v1/suggest) so autocomplete keystrokes are metered against the new searches_suggest bucket separately from full-search volume; ships a drop-in client-side JS handler (jscript_seekmodo_typeahead.js, 150ms debounce, three-section dropdown for keyword / product / category suggestions) and a tenant-side AJAX endpoint (numinix_seekmodo_suggest.php) so unmodified storefronts can opt into Seekmodo-driven typeahead without editing core search templates. Operators can roll back to the v1.0.13 /v1/search typeahead path per-call (opts.use_search=true) or globally (NUMINIX_SEEKMODO_TYPEAHEAD_USE_SEARCH=true) for the cutover window. - v1.0.13 (2026-06-02): pairing is now self-sufficient — the pair-callback flips the connector to enforce mode and forks an initial catalog push automatically, so a freshly-paired storefront is searchable without an operator running install_*_connector.py. Search and indexer cURL timeouts are now separate (search 1500ms, index 30000ms), so a future tenant.snapshot pull can\'t accidentally throttle a bulk catalog push. - v1.0.12 (2026-06-02): public-MCP discovery now writes a real /.well-known/mcp.json file to disk (with a defensive .htaccess) at pair time, on every snapshot poll, and opportunistically once per hour; works on stock cPanel + subdirectory Zen Cart installs without any .htaccess rewrite. - v1.0.11 (2026-06-02): adds public-MCP (anonymous-tier) discovery so AI agents (ChatGPT, Claude, Cursor, Perplexity) can find this storefront\'s product-search endpoint without operator setup; emits a discovery head tag on every storefront page and answers /.well-known/mcp.json when the web server routes it to PHP. - v1.0.10 (2026-06-01): standalone catalog pusher script (numinix_seekmodo_push_catalog.php) lets unmodified storefronts index without a hand-rolled transfer_products.php cron; default filter-mapping registry now covers Zen Cart core SERP filters; ajax-search-suggest clicks are attributed separately as surface=suggest. - v1.0.9 (2026-05-30): zero-touch notifier observer wires NOTIFY_SEARCH_RESULTS, NOTIFY_HEADER_END_ADVANCED_SEARCH_RESULTS, NOTIFY_HEADER_START_PRODUCT_INFO, NOTIFY_CART_ADD_CART_END, NOTIFY_CHECKOUT_PROCESS_AFTER_ORDER_CREATE_ADD_PRODUCTS so storefronts on stock Zen Cart 1.5.8 / 2.0+ work without core file edits. - v1.0.8 (2026-05-29): per-tenant storefront-domain lock (managed at admin.seekmodo.com) short-circuits the connector on non-matching hosts so dev / staging / preview clones can carry the plugin without polluting production. - v1.0.7 (2026-05-26): in-plugin auto-updater (Admin &rarr; Tools &rarr; Seekmodo Updates) with signed-zip verification. - v1.0.6 (2026-05-22): bot-check backend selector. - v1.0.5 (2026-05-18): tenant-wide default-mode + declarative indexer schedule pulled from admin.seekmodo.com.',
